'''Godhuman''' is a [[Fighting Styles|fighting style]] that can be obtained in the [[Third Sea]]. It serves as a superior upgrade to [[Superhuman]], offering enhanced stats and abilities, being one of the reasons it is preferred over most of the fighting styles in PvP.

Godhuman is one of the best [[fighting styles]] in [[PvP mechanics|PvP]] due to its impressive speed, damage, knockback, and stun. It is not at all ideal for grinding because of its slow [M1] attack speed, lack of effective [[Area of Effect|AoE]] moves and high [[mastery]] requirements. Additionally, its knockback is a disadvantage when grinding, as it makes grouping enemies more difficult. In PvP, its main contenders are [[Sanguine Art]] and [[Electric Claw]].

Adding on, disabling screen-shake through the settings greatly improves one of Godhuman's most powerful offenses—the {{Ability|C}}'s held version—making it an extremely reliable combo starter having near-zero repercussions upon landing it.

==Obtainment==
Godhuman is obtainable by learning it from the [[Ancient Monk]]. Upon talking to him, the player will have the opportunity to purchase this fighting style by meeting the following requirements:
* Access to the [[Third Sea]] (Lv. 1500)
* 400+ mastery on all [[fighting styles]] (except [[Sanguine Art]], [[Combat]] and [[Advanced Combat]]) which includes: 
** [[Superhuman]] (requires Mastery 300+ on [[Dark Step]], [[Electric]], [[Water Kung Fu]] and [[Dragon Breath]]).
** [[Death Step]] (requires Mastery 400+ on [[Dark Step]]).
** [[Sharkman Karate]] (requires Mastery 400+ on [[Water Kung Fu]]).
** [[Electric Claw]] (requires Mastery 400+ on [[Electric]]).
** [[Dragon Talon]] (requires Mastery 400+ on [[Dragon Breath]]).
* {{Money|5,000,000}}
* {{Fragment|5,000}}
* {{Dragon Scale|10}} {{Fish Tail|20}} {{Mystic Droplet|10}} {{Magma Ore|20}}

===Tips===

* To efficiently grind all the required [[materials]], the player can use a third party application to automatically click and leave their character at an [[enemy]]'s spawn point while having equipped an [[Elemental]] [[Blox Fruits|fruit]] or [[Buddha]] to not be excessively damaged (note that for enemies with [[Aura]], using a [[Elemental|Elemental fruit]] won't work) and a [[fighting style]] that does not cause the player's character to move during its [M1] attack, such as [[Dark Step]], [[Electric]] and [[Water Kung Fu]].
** Although not recommended due to delay and loss of raw damage, the user can also configure that software to click once each 800ms, which would make the M1s not stack and change according to amount of previous clicks. To get this even more efficient, it's possible to make the game stack the first attacks, but not the dash; by creating a click sequence with different delays. For example, since Dragon Breath dashes at fourth consecutive punch, use the following pattern: `{LMB}; wait 85ms; {LMB}; wait 85ms; {LMB}; wait 800ms`
<!-- Auto-clickers are quite shady in Roblox since although not explicitly banned on ToS, provides advantages over other players and is a third party application, which is banned. Many players believe that is cheating. Consider removing the tip above -->
* Grinding out the fighting styles while leveling normally can get the player Godhuman before reaching the level cap, avoiding have a separate grind for masteries specifically.
** Additionally, it is advisable to focus on grinding [[Magma Ore]]s and [[Fish Tails]] in the [[First Sea]], as the [[NPCs]] in that area are relatively easy to defeat, and the player can also grind all the [[Materials]] while grinding [[Mastery]].
* Using the [[Buddha]] fruit is one of the best technique to do this, as putting [[Stats]] into both [[Fighting Styles|Melee]] and [[health]] when grinding each [[fighting style]] mastery will help gain the mastery quickly.
* Doing [[Sea Events]] in the [[Third Sea]] can be very effective to grind the resources needed for Godhuman as the [[Rumbling Waters]] Event is very common in [[Sea Danger Level]] 5-6 and drop [[Money]] and [[Fragments]].
* A quick and effective way to get mastery is to grind the [[Cocoa Warrior]]s and [[Chocolate Bar Battler]]s as they give around {{EXP|100,000}} every kill, furthermore, both [[NPCs]] can be killed in a loop (group the [[NPCs]] respectively), Cocoa Warriors to Chocolate Bar Battlers to Cocoa Warriors to Chocolate Bar Battlers and repeat. Another option is to grind the [[Cookie Crafter]]s because they are grouped together and are in large numbers, so the player does not need to move around much to defeat these [[NPCs]] and can defeat a lot at once.
** For the strategy above, it's recommended that the user owns [[2x Mastery]] and has a high level.
* Although this requires a very rare enchantment, the user can also use a [[Weapon]] equipped with [[Enchantments#Curses|Curse of the Thief]] to bring [[NPCs]] to them, making grinding mastery a lot easier. 

