==Trivia==
* Godhuman costs {{Money|5,000,000}}, {{Fragment|5,000}}, and will cost {{Money|20,400,000}}, {{Fragment|26,500}} and 3,600 combined [[Mastery|masteries]] from 400 each on all [[Fighting Styles]] except [[Combat]], [[Advanced Combat]] and [[Sanguine Art]].
* Godhuman is the only fighting style to have 2 moves with tap/held variants, with them being {{Ability|X}} and {{Ability|C}}.
* Godhuman is considered the most tedious and time-taking [[fighting styles|Fighting Style]] to obtain by most players, due to it requiring almost every fighting style in the game at 400 mastery along with hard-to-obtain [[Materials|materials]]. In terms of time to obtain this fighting style, it even leaves [[Sanguine Art]] behind. The process might take weeks or even months.
* Godhuman's {{Ability|TAP}} leaves a rainbow trail for a split second, just like how [[Instinct/V2|Instinct V2]] leaves a trail when enabled.
* Like [[Superhuman]], the M1s make a shockwave of compressed air and have a small trail behind when used, Godhuman's being more prominent.
* {{Ability|Z}} and {{Ability|C}} will cause the player to take water damage if their target is below water, so be wary. (Unless the player is using the [[Shark]] race or the user is not using a [[Blox Fruits|Blox Fruit]].)
* {{Ability|Z}} and {{Ability|C}} can allow the player to grab an enemy through a thin wall if their target is close to the wall.
* Godhuman is commonly abbreviated as 'GH' by Blox Fruits players.
* Godhuman is a very versatile and popular [[Fighting Styles|fighting style]] for bounty hunting, and many people use it.
* Godhuman's {{Ability|Z}} and {{Ability|C}} tap variants (as Godhuman's {{Ability|C}} (held) [[Instinct/Break|breaks Instinct]]) themselves are easily "instinct-trickable". It is recommended to use an ability to break or wear off Instinct beforehand, like [[Cyborg]]'s [[Energy Core|V3]] or Godhuman's {{Ability|X}}.
* To see the after images of Godhuman's {{Ability|Godhuman|Z}} (the user has to equip [[Buddha]]) use Godhuman's {{Ability|Godhuman|X}} (tap) and immediately use {{Ability|Godhuman|Z}} to see the after images clearly.
* {{Ability|Z}} deals more damage when hit closer.

